{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/874298-conspiracy-the-adepta-sororitas-oh-yes","id":874298,"title":"Conspiracy: The Adepta Sororitas (Oh yes.)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-25T23:36:17-07:00","id":874298,"title":"Conspiracy: The Adepta Sororitas (Oh yes.)","content":"<div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://pre04.deviantart.net/6cfe/th/pre/f/2009/349/4/a/4a799f17fd56dedd32494096c0d02aab.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i><b>The absence of faith is the mark of the weak.<br /> The absence of faith is the mark of the heretic.<br /> The absence of faith is the mark of damnation.</b><br /> - extract from &quot;The Stern Codex&quot;</i></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">The Adepta Sororitas</span></span></div> ...<br /> <br /> OK, I confess that I have no idea how to write them up; I was planning to convert over the Acts of Faith as their Endowment, but I'm <i>unsure</i> as to how you'd go about making the Sisters of Battle fit. With some tweaking, you could slip them into a Dark Era for Hunters (namely, the Crusades).<br /> <br /> So, yes, suggestions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T03:26:47-07:00","id":874380,"title":"","content":"Making them a Crusades Era Conspiracy (no way they are going to be a Compact) would be pretty interesting, but I'm also open to the idea of making them a modern organization.<br /> <br /> That said, mind giving me a link to some write-ups on those Acts of Faith? I'm having trouble finding them. Alternatively, perhaps they could have Benedictions like the Malleus Maleficarum, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>'s Order of St. Anthony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:15:26-07:00","id":874595,"title":"","content":"They'd also make a good Infinite Macabre Conspiracy, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:06:36-07:00","id":874635,"title":"","content":"They have to be attached to a deity, and so my first thought is a militant arm of the Seers (from Mage), or a cult of subverted Demon Children. Either way, they've embedded themselves in the Catholic Church as an order of Nuns, with only a handful of convents. They technically work with the Maleus, but hold no affiliation with their God or their Benedictions. <br /> <br /> They Hunt Beasts, Demons and Mummies, though anything &quot;Unclean&quot; is their enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:10:11-07:00","id":874637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/874298-conspiracy-the-adepta-sororitas-oh-yes?p=874380#post874380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making them a Crusades Era Conspiracy (no way they are going to be a Compact) would be pretty interesting, but I'm also open to the idea of making them a modern organization.<br /> <br /> That said, mind giving me a link to some write-ups on those Acts of Faith? I'm having trouble finding them. Alternatively, perhaps they could have Benedictions like the Malleus Maleficarum, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>'s Order of St. Anthony.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working on the Acts of Faith from <i>Blood of the Martyrs</i> (one of the Dark Heresy books). They're a bit... darker... than Benedictions, but then again, whipping a crowd into a xeno/mutant/heretic burning frenzy <i>kinda does that</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:26:00-07:00","id":874652,"title":"","content":"That would do the trick. I'd be tempted to have it do something with Azoth or Pyros; as Divine Fire causes fervor and violence.<br /> <br /> Origins wise, the &quot;Evil Church&quot; thing is kind of cliche, but they do need some sort of religious bindings. Maybe borrow from the Cheiron Group and make them an industrial entity. Adepta Solutions is an multinational relief and defense firm, delivering aid workers and security teams to the worst places in the world. They offer scholarships to girls in high schools around the world, after sufficient testing. Adepta sponsors travel abroad, modest accommodations and religious neutrality. As such, they receive millions of dollars in charitable donations, and their security teams boast impressive records.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:55:00-07:00","id":874681,"title":"","content":"Before you consider adapting these women to a Hunter group, you need to consider just what aspects of them you want to carry over. As with any other Warhammer fantasy, part of their sheer appeal is how insanely absurd they are and how straight it's played.<br /> <br /> I mean, an order of monster-hunting warrior-nuns that use holy magic/miracles could work - a sort of feminist contrast to the masculine-dominant/exclusivist Malleus Maleficarum. But fielding disciplined armies of heavily-armored fanatic female war-priests? In the Crusades? You're talking a time period when the Church considered issuing a statement about how big a stick you could legally use to beat your wife with to be progressive. If you take that route, you're going a little beyond even the Old World of Darkness' alternate histories.<br /> <br /> That said... you could potentially use the &quot;female paladins&quot; aspect... if you play it on the down low.<br /> <br /> What I'd suggest is this; the Order of the Bloodied Rose (or whatever name you choose), are a nun's convent who secretly have taken it upon themselves to fight the minions of Satan. In the privacy of their secluded convent, they train in martial practices, learning to wield weapons so they may do battle with the agents of the Devil. The most elite of them all are secretly outfitted in all-concealing armor and sent out to actually do the fighting.<br /> <br /> If you want to make this a Crusades era group, then keep in mind that this convent would need to keep secrecy paramount; there are many powerful figures, secular AND religious, who would decry their existence as unnatural, and heresy of the worst sort. Ironically, you have more freedom to make them an order of warrior-nuns closer to the modern era, when fighting women wouldn't be accused of being demons or witches.<br /> <br /> As for their acts of faith... well, really, that's basically covered by the Benedictions of the MM pretty well, off the top of my head. Since I'm pretty sure nuns tend to be a Catholic thing anyway, you could always just make the group a female branch of the MM; the priests realizing &quot;hey, well, there are some sisters in the faith who would be able to do the Good Lord's work too&quot; and making a place for them.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I were at all inclined to make a magic-using Compact - if this is set in the era of the Crusades, there is no way they'd have the power, numbers or authority to be a Conspiracy, though that might have changed if they survived to the modern era, and 2e is supposedly erasing the &quot;Conspiracies get Endowments and Compacts don't&quot; rule of 1e - based on the Adeptus Soritas, I'd give them pyrotheurgic powers. It visibly seperates them from being more than just &quot;the MM's secret female branch&quot; and reinforces their connection to their inspiration, with their focus on the cleansing, purifying, sanctifying properties of fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:41:03-07:00","id":874742,"title":"","content":"The real distinction between the Sororitas and the Malleus is that the Sororitas <i>aren't</i> spellcasters. They're fanatics who are <i>so</i> fanatical that they can take an artillery shell to the face without flinching... sometimes. The closest thing they get to pyromancy is blessing fire or fuel so it <i>burns people harder</i>.<br /> <br /> I was going to go with &quot;secret convent of warrior nuns&quot; anyway - it does make the most sense. Maybe one where the sisters had a... revelation... about the faith.<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit unsure of <i>who</i> they hunt - part of me wants to say &quot;demonic bloodlines&quot;, so they'd be straight-up antagonistic to the local equivalent of the Lucifuge. But I'm unsure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:53:42-07:00","id":874752,"title":"","content":"Hit on the 40k style enemies. Beasts instead of Orks, fae things instead of Chaos, Mummies instead of Necrons... and so on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:15:20-07:00","id":874773,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking last night that Werewolves are sort of the Space Marines to Hunters Imperial Guard Infantry in regards to the hunt. I like the idea of a Sororitas compact.<br /> <br /> How about instead of a demonic bloodline, they're an angelic bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:32:50-07:00","id":883886,"title":"","content":"Whatever you make them out to be, just make sure that you include some kind free weapons Merit for chainsaws cuz the Sororitas need dem chainswords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}